<onlyinclude>The '''DIKW pyramid''' is a conceptual model that distinguishes data, information, knowledge and wisdom. It often depicts data as the bottom layer and wisdom as the top. The diagram is used to discuss how recorded observations can become useful for understanding and decisions.

== Explanation ==
A list of temperatures is data; a report explaining that a room is overheating provides information; knowing why the heating system fails adds knowledge; choosing an appropriate response involves judgment. These are examples, not universal definitions. Scholars disagree about how the layers relate and whether they form a hierarchy at all.

